9. Conclusion

Software maintenance, reengineering, and Artificial Intelligence play important roles in improving existing software applications.

In the given case study, the college can use corrective, adaptive, perfective, and preventive maintenance to address errors, outdated features, and performance issues in its Student Management System.

Software reengineering can help restructure the existing application, improve its database, and introduce modern functionality without completely rebuilding the system.

AI-assisted code generation, code review, software testing, and bug detection can further support developers in improving software quality and reducing repetitive work.

By combining these approaches, the college can transform its outdated Student Management System into a more efficient, reliable, and user-friendly application that meets modern educational requirements.
